WEBVTT

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:45.100
New F-20 Tiger Shark, a modern, high-performance, multi-role fighter.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:52.270
The Tiger Shark offers free world nations a fighter with the advanced technology features

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:55.510
that give it clear superiority over prospective threats,

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.780
while also providing more capability for less cost than...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:08.740
contemporary fighter aircraft. The F-20 features the General Electric F-404 Advanced Technology

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:16.760
Engine, the same engine that powers the U.S. Navy Marine Corps F-18 Hornet Strike Fighter. In both

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:22.660
testing at General Electric and in flight operations on the Hornet, the F-404 has proven

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:29.970
itself to be an exceptionally rugged, reliable fighter engine. For the single-engine Tiger Shark,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:39.030
An even more reliable version of the F-404 engine has been developed and is performing flawlessly in the F-20 flight test program.

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:48.000
The 17,000-pound thrust-class F-404 engine offers outstanding acceleration and is stall-free.

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:53.280
It is also smokeless, making visual detection difficult.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:59.980
Compared to the earlier generation General Electric J-79 engine, the F-20...

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.270
F404 has 7,700 fewer parts and is 50% lighter.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:11.820
The advanced F404 propulsion system features a modular design.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.190
This means simplicity, high reliability, and low maintenance.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:27.620
Overall, the F404 offers about three times the reliability of the J79.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:36.010
Besides the advanced power plant, the Tiger Shark offers a fully integrated digital avionics system

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:43.080
that provides the aircraft with mission capabilities around the clock and the fastest scramble time of any fighter.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:53.750
The General Electric multi-mode coherent radar greatly enhances the F-20's mission capabilities in both air-to-air and air-to-ground operations.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.980
In an air intercept mission, for example, the Tiger Shark...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.200
pilot can detect and track fighter-size aircraft up to 48 nautical miles away at look-up angles

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:14.870
and up to 31 nautical miles away at look-down angles. In addition to performing search and

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:21.360
track for both look-up and look-down situations, the Tiger Shark radar provides automatic acquisition

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:29.910
and track for air combat. In air-to-surface missions, the F-20

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:38.700
radar provides real beam ground mapping, high-resolution Doppler beam sharpened ground

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:47.560
mapping, and air-to-ground ranging. The F-20 multimode radar offers the highest reliability

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:53.730
of any current fighter radar system, with a mean time between failure of 200 hours.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:59.980
The highly reliable F-20 mission computer provides automatic...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.760
solutions for gun and missile firing.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.220
and bomb release.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.340
The F-20 cockpit is designed around the hands-on stick and throttle.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:10.450
HOSAT,

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:12.830
Head up display.

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:13.810
HUD

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:18.300
and two head down digital display indicators.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.570
POSAT allows the pilot to navigate

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.450
acquire targets and deliver weapons.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.360
without taking his hands off the stick and throttle.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:36.620
The HUD displays weapon, target, and flight data on a clear viewing screen at the pilot's eye level.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.670
Using the HUD or HOSAT,

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:44.170
The Tiger Shark pilot never has to take his eyes off the target at any time.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.290
during an air-to-air combat mission.

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.610
or while making a bombing run at a ground target.

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:54.480
In addition to the standard digital avionics system,

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:58.060
The Tiger Shark is also equipped with such defensive equipment.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:04:59.980
as the ALR-46...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.040
radar warning receiver and the ALE-40 countermeasures dispenser system.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.930
Scramble time is one of the most important yardsticks of any tactical fighter.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:19.910
Scramble time for the Tiger Shark is faster than any other contemporary fighter aircraft.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:25.530
Instead of the conventional electromechanical gyroscopes used in other fighters,

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:29.980
the Tiger Shark offers a Honeywell ring laser gyro inertial.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:30.970
navigation set.

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.640
With the new technology laser navigation set,

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:42.090
Alignment is performed concurrently with startup of the F404 engine.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:45.660
Two and a half minutes after receiving the scramble order,

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:50.330
The F-20 pilot can be airborne at an altitude of 29,000 feet.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.610
13 miles from base,

00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:55.370
flying at a speed of .9 Mach.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.000
with all systems combat ready.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.480
Mean time between failure for the tiger shark navigation set is 2,000 hours.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:11.180
approximately a three-fold improvement over conventional inertial navigation systems in current fighters.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:18.720
Advanced aerodynamic features have been incorporated into the proven Tiger Shark airframe design.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:21.240
These include...

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:23.900
inboard leading edge extensions to the wing.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:25.720
generating greater lift.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.040
large engine inlet ducts.

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:29.930
which provides

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.600
the airflow to enable the F-20 to attain Mach 2 class speeds.

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:41.720
A shark-shaped nose that allows the aircraft to maneuver safely at much higher angles of attack.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:42.980
than current fighters.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.100
The F-20 panoramic canopy

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:52.540
gives the pilot the over-the-shoulder, rearward visibility that is so critical in air-to-air combat.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:59.900
Performance capabilities of the Tiger Shark across the tactical

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.040
mission spectrum, give it the edge over the opponent.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.730
take off in 1,600 feet.

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:21.120
Climb to 40,000 feet in 2.4 minutes from brake release.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.960
faster acceleration in the combat arena than almost any other aircraft.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:30.960
Trapped in a free world.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:33.880
At 10,000 feet.

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.910
from 165 knots

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:39.170
to 505 knots in 28 seconds.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:44.830
from 0.9 Mach to 1.2 Mach in 30 seconds at 30,000 feet.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.040
return rate

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:50.000
Over 11 degrees per second.

00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:53.960
9G maneuver load factor at combat weight.

00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:59.880
The Mach 2 class F-20 flies without restriction on angles.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:08.430
attack or minimum airspeed and is nearly impossible to spin. It can achieve supersonic speed in

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:14.830
military power. In afterburner, the Tiger Shark can maintain high sustained load.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.480
factors well into the supersonic flight regime.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:48.040
These include anti-shipping missiles, conventional weapons, optical and laser-guided ordnance, the Maverick missile, and the new General Electric 30-millimeter gun pod.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:59.800
In addition to its high-performance capabilities, the Tiger Shark has the highest reliability and lowest maintenance requirements of any contemporary fighter in the world.

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.630
The modular design of the engine and avionics systems simplifies maintenance.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.260
reducing time and costs.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:14.930
As a result of being reliable and easy to maintain,

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:19.660
The Tiger Shark has the capability of offering greater combat presence.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:21.840
than any other aircraft in its glass.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.920
The tiger shark uses less fuel than other contemporary fighters.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:29.850
but with equal

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.780
to greater combat persistence.

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.770
The F-20 will have the longest operating life.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.230
at the lowest cost.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.600
of any current high-performance fighter.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.920
The Tiger Shark flight demonstration program is well underway.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:51.750
And all test objectives are being met successfully.

00:10:22.070 --> 00:10:24.310
New F-20 Tiger Shark fighter.

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:27.410
incorporates the most advanced avionics and weapons.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:29.840
with the most modern fighter engine.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:34.240
in the U.S. inventory and a proven aerodynamic design.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.050
at lower life cycle cost than comparable aircraft.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.040
these capabilities.

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:46.860
Put the F-20 Tiger Shark.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.310
in a class by itself.
